    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0077" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34544/707</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-02-26">26 February, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Under Secretary</hi>: As agreed at our
                    conversation yesterday, I enclose herein a memorandum regarding the
                    conversations now going on in London about the bases. This memorandum is of
                    necessity based on rather incomplete information as the Foreign Office have not
                    kept us informed of the details of the negotiations. It is clear, however, from
                    the latest telegrams from the Foreign Office that they are much concerned about
                    the matter and they very much hope that it may be possible for the United States
                    authorities to take action in the sense suggested in the memorandum. I shall be
                    very grateful for any help you may feel able to give.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d52-a1.xml" xpointer="d52-a1"/>
            </div>
